    <!-- Q9 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 9: 秘书反抗的核心对象</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">arms race</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>secretary left him</code>、<code>protestor against the</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P34 Part 3)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          His secretary left him and eventually became a famous <span class="para">protestor against the</span> 9 <span class="ans">[arms race]</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          他的秘书离开了他，最终成为了一名反对【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">军备竞赛（arms race）</span>】的著名抗议者。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P33 Part 3 第1段)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          ...Over the years Bertha von Suttner became increasingly <span class="para">critical of the</span> <span class="ans">arms race</span>. She wrote a famous book, Lay Down Your Arms and became a prominent figure in the <span class="para">peace movement</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          ……多年来，贝尔塔·冯·苏特纳对<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">军备竞赛</span>变得越来越<span style="color:var(--para-color);">持批判态度</span>。她写了一本著名著作《放下武器》，并成为<span style="color:var(--para-color);">和平运动</span>中的杰出人物。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>词性转换</strong>：<code>critical of the arms race</code> 改写为题干 <code>protestor against the [arms race]</code>；</li>
          <li><strong>专有名词提取</strong>：抗议的对象 <code>arms race</code>。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q10: 错题 -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 10: 遗嘱中包含的具体奖项</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">Nobel Peace Prize</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>part of the reason why</code>、<code>included ... in his final will</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P34 Part 3)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          That was part of the reason why Nobel <span class="para">included</span> 10 <span class="ans">[Nobel Peace Prize]</span> <span class="loc">in his final will</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          这就是诺贝尔在<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">最后的遗嘱中</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">包含</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">诺贝尔和平奖</span>】的部分原因。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P33 Part 3 第1段后半)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          No doubt this influenced Alfred Nobel when he wrote <span class="loc">his final will</span> which was to <span class="para">include a Prize for persons or organisations who promoted peace</span>. Several years after the death of Alfred Nobel, the Norwegian Storting (Parliament) decided to award the 1905 <span class="ans">Nobel Peace Prize</span> to Bertha von Suttner.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          毫无疑问，这影响了阿尔弗雷德·诺贝尔写下<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">他的最终遗嘱</span>，其内容是<span style="color:var(--para-color);">设立一个表彰促进和平人士或组织的奖项</span>。诺贝尔去世数年后，挪威议会决定将1905年的<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">诺贝尔和平奖</span>颁发给贝尔塔·冯·苏特纳。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>从句浓缩为专有名词</strong>：原文从句 <code>include a Prize for persons or organisations who promoted peace</code> 对应后文正式官方名称 <code>Nobel Peace Prize</code>；</li>
          <li><strong>因果对标</strong>：<code>No doubt this influenced Alfred Nobel</code> 改写为 <code>That was part of the reason why...</code>。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">错题剖析</span> 你为什么会错写成 <span class="wrong-ans">a prize</span>？</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          <strong>1. 答非所问、核心信息缺失</strong>：诺贝尔遗嘱里有5个奖（物理、化学、医学、文学、和平）。题干上下文完全是因为秘书的和平运动促使他设立的，光写 <code>a prize</code>（一个奖项）根本没有回答出是什么奖！<br>
          <strong>2. 看到短语提前刹车</strong>：原文写 <code>include a Prize for...</code>，你只抄了 <code>a prize</code> 两个词，没有看到后面紧跟的修饰语是指下文的 <code>Nobel Peace Prize</code>。题目允许写不超过3个词，写 <code>Nobel Peace Prize</code> 刚刚好！
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= PASSAGE 1 ================= -->
  <section id="passage-1" class="passage-section">
    <div class="passage-title-bar">
      <h2>Reading Passage 1: The Refrigerator（冰箱的发明）</h2>
      <div class="passage-meta">
        <span>📍 对应位置：PDF P26-P28 / 纸质 P9-P11</span>
        <span>🎯 题型：Summary 单词填写题（Q1-Q6）</span>
        <span>⚠️ 字数限制：ONE WORD ONLY（仅限1个词）</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q1 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 1: 制冷方式的古代起源</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">refrigeration</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>In ancient time</code>、<code>ice and snow</code>、<code>store food</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P28)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          In ancient time, people <span class="para">mainly used</span> <span class="loc">ice and snow</span> <span class="para">as the means of</span> 1 <span class="ans">[refrigeration]</span> <span class="loc">to store food</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          在古代，人们<span style="color:var(--para-color);">主要使用</span><span style="color:var(--locator-color);">冰和雪</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">作为</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">制冷</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">的手段</span>来<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">储存食物</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P26)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Progress took time, however, and <span class="loc">snow and ice</span> <span class="para">served as the primary means of</span> <span class="ans">refrigeration</span> until the beginning of the 20th century.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          然而，进步需要时间，直到 20 世纪初，<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">雪和冰</span>依然<span style="color:var(--para-color);">充当着</span><span style="color:var(--ans-color);">制冷</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">的主要手段</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>句式功能改写</strong>：原文系表结构 <code>served as primary</code> 改写为主动动词短语 <code>mainly used ... as</code>；</li>
          <li><strong>词性转换</strong>：形容词 <code>primary</code> 换副词 <code>mainly</code>；</li>
          <li><strong>原词提取</strong>：介词 <code>of</code> 后直接提取名词 <code>refrigeration</code>。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q2 & Q3 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 2 & 3: 商业制冷的早期应用行业</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">brewing / meatpacking</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>icebox</code>、<code>19th century</code>、<code>commercial refrigeration</code>、<code>industries</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P28)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Then <span class="loc">icebox</span> was introduced during <span class="loc">19th century</span> and <span class="loc">commercial refrigeration</span> <span class="para">was applied to</span> 2 <span class="ans">[brewing]</span> <span class="para">as well as</span> 3 <span class="ans">[meatpacking]</span> <span class="loc">industries</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          随后在 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">19 世纪</span>，<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">冰盒</span>被引入，并且<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">商业制冷</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">被应用到了</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">酿造</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">以及</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">肉类加工</span>】<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">行业</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P26 跨至 P27)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          ...and developed vapor-compression refrigeration <span class="para">for the</span> <span class="ans">brewing</span> <span class="para">and</span> <span class="ans">meatpacking</span> <span class="loc">industries</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          ……并<span style="color:var(--para-color);">为</span><span style="color:var(--ans-color);">酿造</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">和</span><span style="color:var(--ans-color);">肉类加工</span><span style="color:var(--locator-color);">行业</span>开发了蒸汽压缩制冷技术。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>动宾被动扩展</strong>：<code>refrigeration for ... industries</code> 改写为 <code>was applied to ... industries</code>；</li>
          <li><strong>并列连词改写</strong>：<code>and</code> 改写为 <code>as well as</code>。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q4 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 4: 早期有毒冷却剂的更替</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">ammonia</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>In 1859</code>、<code>coolant</code>、<code>poisonous</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P28)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          <span class="loc">In 1859</span>, 4 <span class="ans">[ammonia]</span> <span class="para">replaced air as a coolant</span>, but it was <span class="para">poisonous</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          在 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">1859 年</span>，【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">氨气</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">替代了空气作为冷却剂</span>，但它具有<span style="color:var(--para-color);">毒性</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P27)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          <span class="loc">In 1859</span>, France’s Ferdinand Carré created a more advanced system that <span class="para">used</span> <span class="ans">ammonia</span> <span class="para">as a coolant; the earlier vapor-compression machines used air</span>. The ammonia worked well, but was <span class="para">toxic</span> if it leaked.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          在 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">1859 年</span>，法国的费迪南德·卡雷发明了一种更先进的系统，<span style="color:var(--para-color);">使用</span><span style="color:var(--ans-color);">氨气</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">作为冷却剂；早期的蒸汽压缩机使用的是空气</span>。氨气效果很好，但如果泄漏则具有<span style="color:var(--para-color);">毒性</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>核心同义替换</strong>：<code>toxic</code> 换 <code>poisonous</code>；</li>
          <li><strong>对比浓缩为动词</strong>：用 <code>replaced</code> 概括新旧更替。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q5 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 5: 1920年代更安全的新型制冷剂</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">Freon</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>1920s</code>、<code>safer</code>、<code>took over it</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P28)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The <span class="para">safer</span> 5 <span class="ans">[Freon]</span> <span class="para">took over it</span> in <span class="loc">1920s</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          更<span style="color:var(--para-color);">安全的</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">氟利昂</span>】在 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">20 世纪 20 年代</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">取代了它</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P27)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Engineers worked until the <span class="loc">1920s</span> to come up with <span class="para">better alternatives, one of which was</span> <span class="ans">Freon</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          工程师们一直努力到 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">20 世纪 20 年代</span>才构想出<span style="color:var(--para-color);">更好的替代方案，其中之一就是</span><span style="color:var(--ans-color);">氟利昂（Freon）</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>名词改写为动宾</strong>：<code>better alternatives</code> 改写为 <code>safer took over it</code>。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q6 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 6: 爱因斯坦的绿色发明</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">eco-friendly / greener</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>Even Einstein</code>、<code>inventing ... refrigerator</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句 (PDF P28)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Even <span class="loc">Einstein</span> made contributions <span class="para">by inventing</span> 6 <span class="ans">[eco-friendly]</span> <span class="loc">refrigerator</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          甚至连<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">爱因斯坦</span>也<span style="color:var(--para-color);">通过发明</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">环保</span>】<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">冰箱</span>做出了贡献。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文出处句 (PDF P27)</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Albert <span class="loc">Einstein</span> is remembered for many scientific achievements, but, as Time magazine notes, it’s often overlooked that he also made great <span class="para">contributions to</span> <span class="ans">eco-friendly</span> <span class="loc">refrigeration</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          阿尔伯特·<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">爱因斯坦</span>因许多科学成就而被铭记，但正如《时代》杂志指出的，人们往往忽略了他还为<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">环保</span><span style="color:var(--locator-color);">制冷</span>做出过巨大<span style="color:var(--para-color);">贡献</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>后置修饰转前置定语</strong>：<code>contributions to eco-friendly refrigeration</code> 改写为 <code>inventing [eco-friendly] refrigerator</code>。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= PASSAGE 4 ================= -->
  <section id="passage-4" class="passage-section">
    <div class="passage-title-bar">
      <h2>Reading Passage 4: Tasmanian Tigers（塔斯马尼亚虎 / 袋狼）</h2>
      <div class="passage-meta">
        <span>📍 对应位置：纸质 P27-P30</span>
        <span>🎯 题型：Summary 单词填写（Q1-Q11，一篇到底，无小标题分组）</span>
        <span>📏 字数限制：CHOOSE NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span>
        <span>🏁 本次战绩：11 题对 5 错 6（对 Q1/Q3/Q4/Q7/Q8；错 Q2/Q5/Q6/Q9/Q10/Q11）</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= 本篇总纲 ================= -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.35);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">📐 本篇总纲：Summary 填空题的三步定位法</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">5 / 11</div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">Step 1</span> 划定位词：只划「不会被替换的词」</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          优先级：<span class="loc">数字 / 年份</span> &gt; <span class="loc">大写专有名词</span>（Hobart Zoo、Dingo、DNA）&gt; <span class="loc">学科术语</span>（marsupials、carnivore）&gt; <span class="para">普通名词</span>（stomach、forest）。
          越靠前的词，原文越可能原词照抄；普通名词几乎一定会被改写，只能当"辅助坐标"。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">Step 2</span> 预判词性：空格前后决定填什么</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          <code>a ___ in common</code> → 单数名词（身体部件，不是"动物类别"）；<br>
          <code>in ___</code> → <span class="loc">年份 / 月份 / 地点</span>（Q10 的关键）；<br>
          <code>The ___ destroyed</code> → 句子的<span class="para">施动者（人）</span>，不是动作（Q9 的关键）；<br>
          <code>to ___ a period lack of food</code> → 动词原形（不定式表目的）。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">Step 3</span> 定点回读：定位句 ≠ 答案句</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          本篇 11 题里，<span class="para">7 题</span>的答案<b>不在</b>定位词所在的那半句，而在：
          <b>下一句</b>（Q1）、<b>转折词之后</b>（Q5/Q6）、<b>上一句</b>（Q2）、<b>后置从句/状语之前</b>（Q3）。
          这次 6 道错题，5 道栽在 Step 3。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 一句话记住</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li>定位词负责"把人送到那一行"，<strong>语法与逻辑</strong>负责"在那一行里挑对词"。定位对了却选错词，是 summary 题最高频的失分形态。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="color:#60a5fa; margin-bottom:16px; font-size:16px; border-left:4px solid #3b82f6; padding-left:10px;">
      Part 1: 现代研究与身体构造（Q1-Q4）
    </h3>

    <!-- Q1 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 1: 用骨骼样本 DNA 复制出来的个体</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">clone</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>DNA</code>（学科术语，全文仅 2 处）、<code>bone specimen</code>（骨骼标本）<br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 2 段（P27）→ 扫大写 <code>DNA</code> → 第 3 句 <code>extracted DNA from bones</code> 精准命中 → <b>答案不在这一句</b>，在紧接的下一句 <code>reproduce a clone</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P29 Questions 1-11）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Now many <span class="loc">geneticists</span> <span class="para">assert</span> that they are capable of <span class="para">recreating</span> a 1 <span class="ans">[clone]</span> from <span class="loc">DNA</span> extracted from its <span class="loc">bone specimen</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          如今许多<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">遗传学家</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">断言</span>，他们有能力从骨骼标本中提取的 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">DNA</span> <span style="color:var(--para-color);">重新创造</span>出一个【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">克隆体</span>】。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 2 段第 3 句（P27）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Many <span class="loc">scientists</span> <span class="para">believe</span> that they would be able to <span class="para">reproduce</span> a <span class="ans">clone</span> from the available <span class="loc">DNA</span> of a 136-year-old Thylacine specimen conserved in ethanol since 1866.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          许多<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">科学家</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">认为</span>，他们能够利用一只自 1866 年起就浸泡在乙醇中保存、距今 136 年的袋狼标本中所提取到的可用 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">DNA</span>，<span style="color:var(--para-color);">复制</span>出一个<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">克隆体</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>科学家 → 遗传学家</strong>：<code>scientists</code> ⇄ <code>geneticists</code>（上位词换成具体分支；原文下一句确实出现了 geneticists，属于"同段同义词接力"）；</li>
          <li><strong>认为 → 断言</strong>：<code>believe</code> ⇄ <code>assert</code>（主观认为 → 明确宣称，语气加强，语义不变）；</li>
          <li><strong>复制 → 重新创造</strong>：<code>reproduce</code>（繁殖、复制出生物个体）⇄ <code>recreate</code>（重新创造出来），题干故意用更"造物"的词，弱化"繁殖"的生物学含义；</li>
          <li><strong>136 年标本 → 骨骼标本</strong>：<code>a 136-year-old specimen conserved in ethanol</code> ⇄ <code>bone specimen</code>（原文第 2 段第 2 句已交代 <code>extracted DNA from bones</code>，题干把两句合并压缩）；</li>
          <li><strong>答案位置</strong>：答案紧跟 <code>reproduce</code>，属"动词 + 宾语"型原词落地，最难丢分的一题。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q2: 错题 -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 2: 有袋类动物共有的身体构造</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">pouch</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>marsupials</code>（有袋类，术语，全文 3 处）、<code>in common</code>（共有）<br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：<code>marsupials</code> 三处分别是 ① <code>world's largest marsupial carnivore</code>（第 3 段中）、② <code>unlike other marsupials, the pouch opened at the back</code>（第 3 段末）、③ <code>compared to other marsupials</code>（第 7 段）。<b>只有 ② 带"与其它有袋类不同"的对比结构</b>——有"不同"，才谈得上"共有"，答案就在这里
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Tasmanian tigers <span class="para">belong to</span> <span class="loc">marsupials</span> that have a 2 <span class="ans">[pouch]</span> <span class="para">in common</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          塔斯马尼亚虎<span style="color:var(--para-color);">属于</span><span style="color:var(--locator-color);">有袋类动物</span>，这一类动物<span style="color:var(--para-color);">共同拥有</span>一个【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">育儿袋</span>】。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 3 段末句（P27 最后一行）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The female Tasmanian tiger had a <span class="ans">pouch</span> with four teats but <span class="para">unlike other</span> <span class="loc">marsupials</span>, the <span class="ans">pouch</span> <span class="para">opened at the back</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          雌性塔斯马尼亚虎有一个带四个乳头的<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">育儿袋</span>，但与其它<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">有袋类动物</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">不同的是，这个育儿袋的开口朝后</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>正面陈述 → 反问式共性</strong>：原文只说"雌虎有育儿袋"，题干把它上升为"所有有袋类的共性"——依据是原文的 <code>unlike other marsupials</code>（与其它有袋类不同）。<b>能"不同"的，必然是共有特征</b>；</li>
          <li><strong>差异点 → 共性点</strong>：<code>the pouch opened at the back</code>（袋口朝后 —— 差异）⇄ <code>have a pouch in common</code>（都有育儿袋 —— 共性）。考官把"差异描述"反推成"共性提问"；</li>
          <li><strong>属类关系改写</strong>：<code>belong to marsupials</code> ⇄ 原文通篇的 <code>marsupial</code> 身份（第 3 段 <code>world's largest marsupial carnivore</code>）；</li>
          <li><strong>词性锁死</strong>：<code>a ___ in common</code> = a + 单数名词，必须是"一个可数的身体部件"，不可能是动物类别。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">错题剖析</span> 你写的是 <span class="wrong-ans">carnivore</span>：定位没错，但抓的是"邻居"</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          <strong>1. 你抓到的原文是这一句的上半段</strong>：<code>They had heavy stiff tails, large heads and were the world's largest marsupial <span class="wrong-ans">carnivore</span>.</code> —— <code>marsupial carnivore</code> 里同时出现了 marsupials 的近形词与一个"看起来很专业"的名词，眼睛一扫就锁死了。<br>
          <strong>2. 但 carnivore 回答不了"in common"</strong>：食肉不是有袋类的共性（袋鼠是植食），原文也没说"所有有袋类都食肉"。它是塔斯马尼亚虎<b>区别于</b>其它有袋类的属性，恰好和题干问的"共有"相反。<br>
          <strong>3. 判据是 <code>in common</code> 这个词</strong>：题干只要出现 in common / share / both / all，就必须去找原文里的 <code>unlike / but / whereas</code> 对比句——<b>对比句里被"不同"修饰的那个名词，往往就是"共有"的答案</b>。<br>
          <strong>4. 词性自检也能拦住</strong>：<code>have a carnivore in common</code> 语法上说得通，但语义荒诞（"共同拥有一个食肉动物"）。把候选词代进题干读一遍，2 秒就能否掉。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q3 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 3: 追捕猎物时主要依赖的能力</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">stamina</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>in the chase</code>（追捕，原文原词）、<code>chasing their preys</code>、<code>primarily</code><br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 4 段第 1 句（P28 首行）→ 抓 <code>in the chase</code> 直接命中 → 答案就在 <code>relied on ___ than speed</code> 的中间，与 speed 构成对比
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          When <span class="loc">chasing their preys</span>, these animals <span class="para">primarily depended on</span> 3 <span class="ans">[stamina]</span> <span class="para">to prevail</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          在<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">追捕猎物</span>时，这些动物<span style="color:var(--para-color);">主要依靠</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">耐力</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">来占上风（取胜）</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 4 段第 1 句（P28 首行）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          According to analysis of the skeleton of the Tasmanian Tigers, it has been found that these carnivores <span class="para">mainly relied on</span> <span class="ans">stamina</span> <span class="para">than speed</span> <span class="loc">in the chase</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          根据对塔斯马尼亚虎骨骼的分析，人们发现这些食肉动物在<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">追捕时</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">主要依靠的是</span><span style="color:var(--ans-color);">耐力</span>，<span style="color:var(--para-color);">而非速度</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>介词短语 → 时间状语从句</strong>：<code>in the chase</code>（在追捕中）⇄ <code>When chasing their preys</code>（当追捕猎物时），把名词 chase 还原成动词 chase；</li>
          <li><strong>同义副词</strong>：<code>mainly</code>（主要）⇄ <code>primarily</code>（首要地）；</li>
          <li><strong>同义动词短语</strong>：<code>relied on</code>（依赖）⇄ <code>depended on</code>（依靠）；</li>
          <li><strong>结果型补语</strong>：原文没有 prevail 的对等词，题干用 <code>to prevail</code>（取胜）概括了"靠耐力把猎物拖垮"的整段语义——这是考官加的"目的状语"，不参与定位；</li>
          <li><strong>答案对比结构</strong>：<code>stamina ... than speed</code>（省略了 rather），考查"哪个是主要、哪个是次要"。<b>than 前面的是主项，后面的是陪衬</b>，所以答案是 stamina，speed 是干扰。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">易错提醒</span> speed 是这道题现成的"陪跑选项"</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          原文 <code>relied on stamina than speed</code>（应为 rather than speed）里，speed 与答案只隔一个词，而且"猎豹靠速度"是常识，很容易顺手写 speed。<strong>解法：看到 than / rather than / instead of / not，先判断哪一边是"被肯定"的</strong>——<code>A than B</code> 肯定 A、否定 B，答案在 than 之前。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q4 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 4: 一次吃很多是为了应对什么</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">compensate（原文 compensating）</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>stomach</code>（胃，连续两句出现）、<code>food scarcity</code>（食物匮乏）<br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 4 段第 2-3 句（P28）→ 第 2 句讲"胃能扩张、一次吃很多"，第 3 句 <code>The stomachs were adapted ... for compensating ...</code> 才是答案句。<b>题干把两句压成一句，答案在第 3 句</b>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Their <span class="loc">stomach</span> could <span class="para">inflate</span> so they could <span class="para">eat large amount of food each time</span> to 4 <span class="ans">[compensate for]</span> <span class="para">a period lack of food</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          它们的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">胃</span>能够<span style="color:var(--para-color);">膨胀</span>，因此它们可以<span style="color:var(--para-color);">一次吃下大量食物</span>，以【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">补偿</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">一段缺乏食物的时期</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 4 段第 2-3 句（P28）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The <span class="loc">stomach</span> of the tigers was muscular and had an ability to <span class="para">distend</span> for allowing the animal to <span class="para">eat huge amount of food at one time</span>. The stomachs were adapted in a way for <span class="ans">compensating</span> <span class="para">longer period without eating</span> when the tigers failed to hunt and during <span class="loc">food scarcity</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          这种虎的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">胃</span>肌肉发达，具有<span style="color:var(--para-color);">扩张</span>能力，使这种动物能够<span style="color:var(--para-color);">一次吃下巨量食物</span>。它们的胃以这样的方式适应环境：在捕猎失败以及<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">食物匮乏</span>、<span style="color:var(--para-color);">长时间无法进食</span>时进行<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">补偿</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>inflate ⇄ distend</strong>：都表示"膨胀、鼓起"，distend 更偏医学/解剖语境（胃壁被撑开）；</li>
          <li><strong>large amount ⇄ huge amount</strong>：同义数量短语，只换形容词；<code>each time</code> ⇄ <code>at one time</code>（每次 ⇄ 一次）；</li>
          <li><strong>a period lack of food ⇄ longer period without eating / food scarcity</strong>：题干把原文的两个并列状语（长时间不进食 + 食物匮乏）合并成一个名词短语；</li>
          <li><strong>动词形式</strong>：原文 <code>for compensating</code>（介词 + 动名词）⇄ 题干 <code>to compensate for</code>（不定式表目的）。<b>for + doing 与 to do 是同一目的状语的两种写法</b>，这一步转换决定了答案要写成动词原形 compensate（介词 for 可带可不带，写 compensate for 最稳）。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title">⚠️ 本题出题瑕疵：答案词形被迫改动</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          原文是 <b>for compensating</b>（介词 + 动名词），题干改成了 <b>to ___</b>（不定式），所以答案只能从 <b>compensating</b> 变形为 <b>compensate</b>。<br>
          但雅思阅读的铁律是<b>原样照抄</b>：不改时态、不改单复数、不改词性、不换同义词。所以正确逻辑应该反过来用——<b>如果你找到的词填进空格后语法不通，说明你找错了句子</b>，而不是自己去变形。<br>
          同一处改写还留下了第二个疤：题干 <code>a period lack of food</code> 本身不合英语语法（应为 <code>a period of food shortage</code>）。正规剑桥题会把空放在 <code>for ___ longer periods without eating</code> 的位置，让 compensating 原样填进去。<br>
          第三处不自洽：<b>compensate 表"补偿"时必须带 for</b>，而题干空格后面并没有印 for，所以严格按语法应写 <code>compensate for</code>（两词，仍在 THREE WORDS 限内）；答案键只给 compensate 是编辑疏忽。<br>
          <b>结论：本题按题干写 compensate for 最保险，但别把"自己改词形"学成做题习惯。</b>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="color:#60a5fa; margin-top:35px; margin-bottom:16px; font-size:16px; border-left:4px solid #3b82f6; padding-left:10px;">
      Part 2: 食性、天敌与灭绝（Q5-Q11）
    </h3>

    <!-- Q5 -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 5: 导致人类大规模捕杀的食物（一）</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">sheep</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>twentieth century</code>（世纪，数字类）、<code>mass killing</code>（原文原词）、<code>diet</code><br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 6 段（P28）→ 先扫 <code>mass killing</code> 锁定末句 → <b>往前退一句</b>，找"为什么会被杀"：<code>because these carnivores mainly ate the sheep and poultry</code>。<b>注意不是段首那一长串食物清单</b>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P29-30）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The <span class="loc">diet</span> of the Tasmanian tiger included the 5 <span class="ans">[sheep]</span> and 6 <span class="ans">[poultry]</span>, and <span class="para">this resulted in</span> <span class="loc">mass killing</span> of the tigers by people in the <span class="loc">twentieth century</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          塔斯马尼亚虎的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">食谱</span>包括【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">羊</span>】和【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">家禽</span>】，<span style="color:var(--para-color);">而这导致了</span> 20 世纪人类对它们的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">大规模捕杀</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 6 段（P28）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The food list of the Tasmanian Tiger included kangaroos, wombats, birds, wallabies and small animals like potoroos and possums. ... <span class="para">However</span>, these tigers were considered a blood drinker in the <span class="loc">twentieth century</span> <span class="para">because</span> these carnivores mainly ate the <span class="ans">sheep</span> and <span class="ans">poultry</span> of the farmers. Their bad reputation <span class="para">led to</span> <span class="loc">mass killing</span> of Tigers by humans.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          塔斯马尼亚虎的食物清单包括袋鼠、袋熊、鸟类、小袋鼠，以及像鼠袋鼠和负鼠这样的小型动物。……<span style="color:var(--para-color);">然而</span>，在 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">20 世纪</span>，这种虎被视为"嗜血者"，<span style="color:var(--para-color);">因为</span>它们主要吃农民的<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">羊</span>和<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">家禽</span>。它们的坏名声<span style="color:var(--para-color);">导致</span>了人类对虎的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">大规模捕杀</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>food list ⇄ diet</strong>：具体清单 ⇄ 抽象"食谱"，这一层改写把段落前半段的袋鼠/袋熊全部划进了 <code>diet</code> 的范围 —— <b>这正是本题最大的陷阱</b>；</li>
          <li><strong>mainly ate ⇄ included</strong>：题干用"包括"弱化了原文的"主要吃"，让列举项看起来同样合法；</li>
          <li><strong>led to ⇄ resulted in</strong>：导致（同义动词短语，因果方向一致）；</li>
          <li><strong>bad reputation 被删掉</strong>：原文的因果链是三段（吃羊 → 坏名声 → 被杀），题干压成两段（吃羊 → 被杀），中间环节删除，<b>by people / by humans 一一对应</b>；</li>
          <li><strong>答案位置</strong>：<code>the sheep and poultry of the farmers</code> —— <code>the</code> 后面的 sheep 对应第 5 空，and 后面的 poultry 对应第 6 空，<b>词序与空格编号严格一致</b>，这是 summary 双空题的固定规律。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">错题剖析</span> 你写的是 <span class="wrong-ans">kangaroos, wombats, birds</span> / <span class="wrong-ans">small animals</span>：清单抓对了，因果抓错了</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          <strong>1. 你抄的是"食谱"，题干问的是"死因"</strong>：段首那一长串（kangaroos, wombats, birds, wallabies, potoroos, possums）确实是 diet，但它<b>不产生</b> mass killing —— 吃野生动物不会让农民悬赏杀虎，吃羊和家禽才会。<br>
          <strong>2. <code>However</code> 是分界线</strong>：原文用 However 把段落劈成两半，前半是"自然食谱"（无争议），后半是"与人的冲突"（致祸原因）。<b>题干里只要出现 result in / lead to / cause / because，就必须跳到转折词之后去找</b>。<br>
          <strong>3. <code>because</code> 后面才是答案</strong>：<code>because these carnivores mainly ate the <span class="ans">sheep</span> and <span class="ans">poultry</span> of the farmers</code> —— 一个 because 直接给出因果，答案就是它紧跟的两个名词。<br>
          <strong>4. 双空题的编号对应</strong>：题干 <code>the 5 ___ and 6 ___</code>，原文 <code>the sheep and poultry</code> —— the 对 5、and 对 6，位置完全平行。如果两个空填成同一类东西（如 kangaroos 和 small animals，后者是前者的总称），基本可以判定抓错了层级。<br>
          <strong>5. 字数也报警了</strong>：kangaroos, wombats, birds 已经是 3 个词，把一整串列举塞进一个空，本身就违背了"ONE WORD"的命题习惯（本篇虽允许 3 词，但答案通常是 1-2 词的具体名词）。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q7 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 7: 面对敌人时几乎不做的事</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">resistance</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>die out of fear</code>（原文原词，全篇唯一）、<code>captured</code><br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 7 段（P28）→ <code>die out of fear and shock</code> 一眼命中 → 答案在<b>紧接的下一句</b>：<code>They hardly used to put up some resistance before their enemies</code>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P30）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          They <span class="para">seldom</span> <span class="para">set up</span> some 7 <span class="ans">[resistance]</span> <span class="para">in front of the foes</span> and used to <span class="loc">die out of fear</span> when <span class="loc">captured</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          它们<span style="color:var(--para-color);">很少</span>在敌人面前<span style="color:var(--para-color);">做出</span>任何【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">抵抗</span>】，并且在被<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">捕获</span>时会因<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">恐惧而死去</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 7 段第 3-4 句（P28）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          When they were <span class="loc">captured</span>, they used to <span class="loc">die out of fear</span> and shock. They <span class="para">hardly</span> used to <span class="para">put up</span> some <span class="ans">resistance</span> <span class="para">before their enemies</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          被<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">捕获</span>时，它们常常因<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">恐惧</span>和惊吓而死。它们几乎不会在<span style="color:var(--para-color);">敌人面前</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">做出</span>任何<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">抵抗</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>句子顺序调换</strong>：原文先说"被捕获时吓死"，后说"不抵抗"；题干把两句<b>前后对调</b>（先不抵抗、再吓死）。定位词 die out of fear 因此落在题干<b>末尾</b>，答案反而在它<b>前面一句</b>——这是本题唯一的时间成本；</li>
          <li><strong>hardly ⇄ seldom</strong>：否定副词互换（几乎不 ⇄ 很少），两个都带否定含义，语义等价；</li>
          <li><strong>put up ⇄ set up</strong>：<code>put up resistance</code> 是固定搭配"进行抵抗"，题干换成 set up（建立），属于<b>搭配词被替换、核心名词保留</b>；</li>
          <li><strong>before their enemies ⇄ in front of the foes</strong>：enemies → foes（同义名词，foes 更书面）、before → in front of（介词短语化）；</li>
          <li><strong>答案核心</strong>：<code>some resistance</code>，some + 不可数名词，与题干 <code>some ___</code> 完全对齐。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q8 -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 8: 争夺栖息地与食物的竞争物种</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">Dingo</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>rival</code>（竞争者）→ 原文对应 <code>competed for</code>；<code>habitats and food sources</code> → 原文 <code>food and shelter</code>；<code>Australia</code>（大写）<br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 8 段（P28-29）→ 段首 <code>It is believed that ... Australia</code> 就是本段唯一讲"另一个物种"的段落 → 答案是被 <code>called</code> 引出的那个大写专名
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P30）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Another kind of <span class="loc">wild animal</span> called 8 <span class="ans">[Dingo]</span> was its <span class="para">rival for</span> <span class="loc">habitats and food sources</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          另一种被称为【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">澳洲野犬（Dingo）</span>】的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">野生动物</span>，是它在<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">栖息地和食物来源</span>上的<span style="color:var(--para-color);">竞争者</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 8 段（P28 末 - P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          It is believed that the fierce and <span class="loc">wild</span> hunters of Australia, <span class="ans">Dingo</span> is somehow responsible for the extinction of the Tasmanian tigers. These <span class="loc">wild dogs</span> may have <span class="para">competed for</span> <span class="loc">food and shelter</span> with the Thylacine resulting in the death of the tigers from areas like Papua New Guinea and Australian mainland.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          人们认为，澳大利亚凶猛的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">野生</span>猎手——<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">澳洲野犬</span>，在某种程度上对塔斯马尼亚虎的灭绝负有责任。这些<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">野狗</span>可能与袋狼<span style="color:var(--para-color);">争夺</span>过<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">食物和栖身之处</span>，导致新几内亚和澳大利亚大陆等地区的这种虎死亡。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>competed for ⇄ rival for</strong>：动词短语（为……竞争）⇄ 名词 + 介词（……的竞争者）。<b>词性转换题</b>：原文动词谓语被压成题干的名词表语；</li>
          <li><strong>food and shelter ⇄ habitats and food sources</strong>：shelter（栖身之处）被升级为 habitats（栖息地），food 被扩成 food sources（食物来源）。<b>上位词替换</b>，语义范围变大但指同一件事；</li>
          <li><strong>wild dogs ⇄ wild animal</strong>：具体种类 ⇄ 上位类别；fierce and wild hunters ⇄ wild animal 也是同一条思路；</li>
          <li><strong>答案引出方式</strong>：<code>called</code> 对应原文的同位语 <code>the fierce and wild hunters of Australia, Dingo</code>——<b>逗号 + 大写专名 = 同位语</b>，答案就在逗号后。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">易错提醒</span> 大小写是白送的分</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          本篇唯一一个大写专名答案就是 Dingo，抄写时<b>首字母必须大写</b>。另外别写成 <span class="wrong-ans">wild dogs</span> 或 <span class="wrong-ans">Thylacine</span>：题干已经说了 <code>another kind of wild animal</code>（"另一种"），Thylacine 是它自己，答案只能是"另一个物种的名字"。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q9: 错题 -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 9: 砍伐森林、开垦农田的施动者</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">European settlers</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>forests and grassland</code>（原文原词，仅 1 处）、<code>could not cope with</code>（原文原词）<br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 9 段（P28 末 - P29 首）→ 抓 <code>much of the forests and grasslands were cleared</code> 命中 → <b>但原文是被动句，施动者被省略</b>，必须回读同一句的 <code>after the European settlers started inhabiting ...</code> 才能补出主语
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P30）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The 9 <span class="ans">[European settlers]</span> <span class="para">destroyed</span> the <span class="loc">forests and grassland</span> where the tigers lived, and these native animals <span class="loc">could not cope with</span> <span class="para">this change</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">欧洲移民</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">毁掉了</span>虎所栖息的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">森林和草原</span>，而这些本土动物<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">无法应对</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">这一变化</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 9 段（P28 末 - P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          In the early 18th century, after the <span class="ans">European settlers</span> started inhabiting most of the lands in the Australian mainland and in Tasmania, much of the <span class="loc">forests and grasslands</span> <span class="para">were cleared</span> so that they could be converted to farmlands. This movement led to a huge clash between the settlers and the native animals who <span class="loc">could not cope with</span> <span class="para">the environmental situation</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          18 世纪初，在<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">欧洲移民</span>开始占据澳大利亚大陆和塔斯马尼亚的大部分土地之后，大片<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">森林和草原</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">被清除</span>，以便改造成农田。这一举动导致移民与本土动物之间的巨大冲突，这些本土动物<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">无法应对</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">这种环境状况</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>被动 → 主动（施动者补全）</strong>：原文 <code>the forests were cleared</code>（森林被清除，施动者隐身）⇄ 题干 <code>The ___ destroyed the forests</code>（要求填施动者）。<b>这是本题的命门</b>：原文根本没写"谁砍的"，只能从上一分句 <code>after the European settlers started inhabiting</code> 推出；</li>
          <li><strong>were cleared ⇄ destroyed</strong>：清除（中性农事动作）⇄ 摧毁（带负面评价）。考官故意换成语义更重的词，暗示"这是灭绝主因"；</li>
          <li><strong>this change ⇄ the environmental situation</strong>：具体变化 ⇄ 抽象环境状况，概括化改写；</li>
          <li><strong>could not cope with</strong>：<b>原词照抄</b>，这是全篇最强的定位锚点（4 个词的完整短语，几乎不会换）；</li>
          <li><strong>答案形态</strong>：题干 <code>The ___</code> + 谓语 destroy，要求<b>能主动毁林的"人"</b>，所以必须是 <code>European settlers</code>（2 词），不能是 farmlands（农田是被改造的结果）、forests（被毁的对象）。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">错题剖析</span> 你写的是 <span class="wrong-ans">european</span>：方向对了，但只抄了半截</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          <strong>1. 语义没跑偏，是"抄漏了中心词"</strong>：原文的完整名词短语是 <code>European settlers</code>（欧洲<b>移民</b>），european 只是形容词。题干 <code>The ___ destroyed ...</code> 的主语中心词必须是名词，单写 European 等于"那个欧洲人"，把人称和数量都说错了。<br>
          <strong>2. 考官允许 3 个词，这里正好用得上</strong>：<code>European settlers</code> 2 词，完全在 NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS 之内。凡是原文出现"形容词 + 名词"的固定称谓（European settlers / native animals / wild dogs），<b>一律连抄</b>，不要只抄形容词。<br>
          <strong>3. 若答案只给一个词，最可能是 settlers</strong>：有些版本的答案为 <code>settlers</code>。无论哪种，核心名词都不能丢。<br>
          <strong>4. 定位路径上的教训</strong>：<code>The ___ destroyed</code> 这种"主语空"，必须做一件事——<b>把被动句还原成主动句，问一句"是谁干的？"</b>。原文用 <code>after the European settlers started inhabiting</code> 交代施动者，用 <code>were cleared</code> 交代动作，两者分居同一句的首尾，中间隔了 12 个词。这就是"定位到了却填不出"的典型结构。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q10: 错题 + 数字规则 -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 10: 最后一只虎死于霍巴特动物园的年份</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">1936</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>Hobart Zoo</code>（双大写专名，全文唯一）、<code>The last Tasmanian tiger</code>（段首主题句）<br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 11 段第 1 句（P29）→ <code>Hobart Zoo</code> 零竞争命中 → 同一句有两个数字：<code>1933</code>（被捕获）与 <code>1936</code>（死亡）。题干问 <b>perished（死亡）</b>，取后者
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P30）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The last Tasmanian tiger <span class="para">perished</span> in the <span class="loc">Hobart Zoo</span> in 10 <span class="ans">[1936]</span> and this <span class="para">marked the termination</span> to this species.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          最后一只塔斯马尼亚虎在 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">霍巴特动物园</span>【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">1936 年</span>】<span style="color:var(--para-color);">死亡</span>，这<span style="color:var(--para-color);">标志着</span>该物种的终结。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 11 段第 1 句（P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          The last Tasmanian tiger was captured in <span class="loc">1933</span> and was kept in the <span class="loc">Hobart Zoo</span> but it <span class="para">died</span> three years later in <span class="ans">1936</span> <span class="para">making an end to</span> this species.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          最后一只塔斯马尼亚虎于 <span style="color:var(--locator-color);">1933 年</span>被捕获，饲养在<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">霍巴特动物园</span>，但三年后于<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">1936 年</span><span style="color:var(--para-color);">死去</span>，从而<span style="color:var(--para-color);">终结了</span>这个物种。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>died ⇄ perished</strong>：死（中性）⇄ 消亡（书面、含"物种灭绝"重量感）；</li>
          <li><strong>making an end to ⇄ marked the termination to</strong>：结束 ⇄ 标志着终结（动词短语 → 动宾结构，语气正式化）；</li>
          <li><strong>两个数字的分工</strong>：<code>1933</code> = 被捕获（captured），<code>1936</code> = 死亡（died）。题干动词换了词（perished ⇄ died），<b>考点就是"哪个动作对应哪个年份"</b>，不是"抄哪个数字"；</li>
          <li><strong>three years later 是"桥"，不是答案</strong>：它是从句 1933 到 1936 的推算说明（1933 + 3 = 1936），在句中作时间状语，与题干 <code>in ___</code> 的坑位不对应。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box" style="background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.08); border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.35);">
        <div class="logic-title" style="color: var(--para-color);">📏 你的疑问：题目没说 "AND/OR A NUMBER"，到底能不能填数字？</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><b>能填，而且必须填。</b>雅思官方规则：<b>数字用阿拉伯数字写，算 1 个词</b>（1936 = one word，nineteen thirty-six 也只是把它展开，同样只算 1 个）。"NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS" 限制的是<b>词数</b>，不是<b>词性/词类</b>，年份、百分比、金额都在允许范围内。</li>
          <li><b>"NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER" 只是写得更明确</b>，并不代表"只写 WORDS 的题就不能填数字"。剑桥真题里大量 answers 就是纯数字（如 <i>£480</i>、<i>1936</i>、<i>10%</i>），对应的 rubric 常常只写 NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS。</li>
          <li><b>真正的失分点不是"能不能填数字"，而是"填了哪个数字"</b>：题干 <code>in ___</code> 要的是<b>年份</b>，你写 tree（three 的近音误记）/ three years later，是"时间间隔"而不是"年份"，坑位与词性都不匹配。</li>
          <li><b>可迁移的判据：题干介词 = 答案类型</b>。<code>in</code> + 年/月/季；<code>by</code> + 不晚于某时间；<code>at</code> + 时点/地点；<code>to</code> + 方向/对象；<code>with</code> + 工具/伴随。看到 in 就先在原文里锁定"年份级"信息，其余数字自动降级为干扰。</li>
          <li><b>形近词提醒</b>：three /θriː/ 与 tree /triː/ 只差一个 /θ/，抄写时把 three 写成 tree 是"音形脱节"，不是听力问题——写完回读一遍题干，<code>in tree</code> 立刻就能自查出来。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">错题剖析</span> 你写的是 <span class="wrong-ans">tree（three years later）</span>：抄了状语，丢了年份</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          <strong>1. 语义层级抓错</strong>：<code>three years later</code> 回答的是"多久之后死的"，题干问的是"哪一年死的"。一个问 duration，一个问 date，<b>不能互换</b>。<br>
          <strong>2. 同句双数字必须做"动作配对"</strong>：captured → 1933，died → 1936。题干用的是 perished，属"死亡"一列，所以取 1936。做题时在同句看到两个数字，先在草稿上写 <code>1933=captured / 1936=died</code>，再回头对题干动词，10 秒解决。<br>
          <strong>3. 别怕数字</strong>：本篇 11 个答案里有 1 个是数字，而 Q5/Q6 的双空、Q9 的复合名词都在 3 词以内——<b>字数限制宽松时，答案的"形态"由题干语法决定，不由你偏好决定</b>。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Q11: 错题 -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">Question 11: 被大量报告但都未被证实的东西</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">sightings</div>
      </div>
      <div class="locator-line">
        🎯 <strong>黄金定位词</strong>：<code>reported</code>（原文原词）、<code>none ... confirmed</code>（否定 + 证实）、<code>Until now</code> ⇄ <code>So far</code><br>
        🧭 <strong>定位路径</strong>：第 11 段<b>倒数第 2 句</b>（P29）→ 先扫段末的 <code>none has been confirmed</code> 锁定句群 → 答案在 <code>reported</code> 与 <code>of Tasmanian tigers</code> <b>之间</b>，是被 report 的那个名词
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">1. 题干检索点</span> 考官题干句（P30）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          <span class="para">So far</span> <span class="para">lots of</span> 11 <span class="ans">[sightings]</span> of the tigers have been <span class="loc">reported</span>, but none of them has been <span class="para">proven</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          <span style="color:var(--para-color);">到目前为止</span>，已有<span style="color:var(--para-color);">大量</span>关于这种虎的【<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">目击记录</span>】被<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">报告</span>，但没有一起得到<span style="color:var(--para-color);">证实</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">2. 原文事实点</span> 原文第 11 段倒数第 2 句（P29）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          <span class="para">Until now</span>, there have been <span class="para">hundreds of</span> <span class="loc">reported</span> <span class="ans">sightings</span> of Tasmanian tigers but none has been <span class="para">confirmed</span>.
        </div>
        <div class="zh-text">
          <span style="color:var(--para-color);">直到现在</span>，已有<span style="color:var(--para-color);">数百起</span>关于塔斯马尼亚虎的<span style="color:var(--locator-color);">被报告</span>的<span style="color:var(--ans-color);">目击事件</span>，但没有一起得到<span style="color:var(--para-color);">证实</span>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 考官改写逻辑</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><strong>Until now ⇄ So far</strong>：直到现在 ⇄ 到目前为止（时间状语同义替换，本句最稳的定位锚）；</li>
          <li><strong>hundreds of ⇄ lots of</strong>：数百 ⇄ 大量（具体数量 → 模糊数量，考官常把数字虚化）；</li>
          <li><strong>confirmed ⇄ proven</strong>：被证实 ⇄ 被证明（同义过去分词，被动结构不变）；</li>
          <li><strong>词性转换（关键）</strong>：原文 <code>reported</code> 是<b>形容词</b>修饰 sightings；题干把它变成<b>被动谓语</b> <code>have been reported</code>，于是 <code>sightings</code> 从"被修饰的中心词"升级为"被报告的对象"，<b>答案的位置从 reported 之后移到了 reported 之前/之间</b>；</li>
          <li><strong>答案锁定</strong>：题干 <code>lots of ___ of the tigers</code> = 原文 <code>hundreds of reported sightings of Tasmanian tigers</code>——去掉修饰语 reported，剩下的中心名词就是答案 <code>sightings</code>（复数不可丢 s）。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trap-box">
        <div class="trap-title"><span class="badge badge-warn">错题剖析</span> 你写的是 <span class="wrong-ans">media</span>：抓了上一句的"名人词"</div>
        <div class="trap-content">
          <strong>1. media 在上一句，且不是"被报告的对象"</strong>：原文是 <code>The Australian <span class="wrong-ans">media</span> became so anxious ... that they even offered a reward of 1 million dollars</code>——媒体是"悬赏的一方"（施动者），不是"被 report 的东西"。<br>
          <strong>2. 代入题干立刻语病</strong>：<code>lots of media ... have been reported</code>（大量媒体被报告）在语义上讲不通。<b>填完必做"代入回读"</b>，5 秒就能否掉。<br>
          <strong>3. 真正的定位结构是"but 后的否定"</strong>：题干 <code>but none of them has been proven</code> 与原文 <code>but none has been confirmed</code> 几乎逐词对应，<b>这是全篇最"送分"的定位句</b>。抓住 but + none + 被动完成时，就能一步落到句子上。<br>
          <strong>4. 深层原因：名词单复数与"事件名词"不熟</strong>：sighting 是"目击（事件）"，考生对它的名词化用法不敏感，听到/读到 <code>reported sightings</code> 会本能跳过，转而去抓更"眼熟"的 media。这类"熟词优先"的注意力偏移，是 summary 题失分的第二大原因（仅次于定位句≠答案句）。
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= 本篇会诊 ================= -->
    <div class="card" style="border-color: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4);">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div class="q-title">🩺 本篇错题会诊：6 道错题，4 类病根</div>
        <div class="q-ans-pill">5 / 11 → 目标 9+</div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">病根 1</span> 抓"邻居词"：定位对了，词选错了（Q2、Q11）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Q2 抓了上一行末尾的 <span class="wrong-ans">carnivore</span>，Q11 抓了上一句的 <span class="wrong-ans">media</span>。共同点：<b>都是紧邻答案句的"专业/名人词"，看起来比答案更"像答案"</b>。<br>
          <b>解法</b>：填完把候选词代回题干读一遍。carnivore 代进去 → "共同拥有一个食肉动物"（荒谬）；media 代进去 → "大量媒体被报告"（荒谬）。<b>2 秒代入法，能拦住本篇 2 道错题。</b>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">病根 2</span> 因果链断在转折词上（Q5、Q6）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          题干有 <span class="para">result in / lead to / because</span> 时，答案几乎必然在 <span class="para">However / But / because / so</span> 之后。你在段首的食物清单上停住了，没跨过 <code>However</code>。<br>
          <b>解法</b>：读到 summary 句子里出现因果词，先在原文该段<b>找转折词</b>，再从转折词往后读两句——这两句里必有一个是答案句。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-stem"><span class="badge badge-q">病根 3</span> 题干语法没用来筛词（Q9、Q10）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          Q9 题干 <code>The ___ destroyed</code> 要"施动者名词"，你只抄了形容词 european；Q10 题干 <code>in ___</code> 要"年份"，你抄了时间状语 three years later。<br>
          <b>解法</b>：<b>先决定"我要找什么"，再去找</b>。做题顺序应该是「读题干 → 判词性/判类型（人？年？身体部件？动作？）→ 回原文捞」，而不是「回原文看到像的就抄」。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <div class="block-header header-orig"><span class="badge badge-orig">病根 4</span> 双空题不按编号对位（Q5、Q6 连带）</div>
        <div class="en-text">
          题干 <code>the 5 ___ and 6 ___</code> 与原文 <code>the sheep and poultry</code> 是<b>严格平行</b>的结构（the → 5，and → 6）。只要发现两个空的答案"是同一类东西的上下位关系"（kangaroos 与 small animals），就该立刻怀疑抓错了层级。<br>
          <b>解法</b>：双空题先在原文把"the A and B"整块圈出来，再分别落位，<b>绝不跨句各抓一个</b>。
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="logic-box">
        <div class="logic-title">⚡ 下一步训练（本篇专项，20 分钟）</div>
        <ul class="logic-list">
          <li><b>第一遍（5 分钟）</b>：只看题干，把 11 个空各自的"答案类型"写在旁边（人/年/身体部件/动作/动物名/复数名词）。写完再回原文，不许边读边填。</li>
          <li><b>第二遍（8 分钟）</b>：只做 Q2、Q5、Q6、Q9、Q10、Q11 六题，强迫自己在定位句上画两笔——一笔圈转折词，一笔圈题干对应的语法槽位。</li>
          <li><b>第三遍（7 分钟）</b>：把本篇 20 组替换（见下表）遮住中文，只看英文，口头说出"题干词 → 原文词"，说不出来的做记号，进改写本。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

